== From Vacuum Theory to Material Engineering ==

[[ψ Dispersion Relations]] (A3) derived the coherence length in vacuum:

:<math>L_\psi^{\rm vac} = \frac{1}{m_{\rm eff,vac}}, \qquad m_{\rm eff,vac}^2 = m^2 + 3\lambda\psi_0^2</math>

This is a vacuum result — it gives L_ψ in the absence of any material. Inside a real composite, [[ψ Constitutive Relations]] (B1) shows that the modified wave equation replaces the vacuum d'Alembertian with a material-modified version, shifting the effective mass:

:<math>m_{\rm eff,mat}^2 = \varepsilon_\psi\mu_\psi\,m_{\rm eff,vac}^2</math>

Therefore:

:<math>\boxed{L_\psi^{\rm mat} = \frac{1}{m_{\rm eff,mat}} = \frac{L_\psi^{\rm vac}}{\sqrt{\varepsilon_\psi\mu_\psi}}}</math>

{{Math_Bridge
