| in_english     =
* <math>L_\psi^{\rm mat}</math> — the coherence length inside the composite: how far the static ψ field reaches from any source point within the material.
* <math>L_\psi^{\rm vac}</math> — vacuum coherence length, set by the bare mass <math>m</math>. This is calibrated at TML-1 by measuring the resonant frequency shift of the empty cavity vs filled cavity.
* <math>\varepsilon_\psi</math> — ψ permittivity of the composite. Both BST and polymer fill increase <math>\varepsilon_\psi > \varepsilon_0</math>, reducing <math>L_\psi</math> (from [[ψ Permittivity]] B2).
* <math>\mu_\psi</math> — ψ permeability, tunable via ferrofluid H-field (from [[ψ Permeability]] B3). This is the primary control variable.
* '''Key insight:''' The <math>\varepsilon_\psi</math> contribution is approximately fixed by the composite formulation. The <math>\mu_\psi</math> contribution is tunable in real time. Therefore: <math>L_\psi \propto 1/\sqrt{\mu_\psi(H)}</math> for a fixed composite, with H-field as the engineering control variable.
