== The Yukawa Spatial Profile ==

The coherence length directly gives the spatial profile of any static ψ source. For a point source of ψ charge <math>Q_\psi</math> at the origin, inside a material with coherence length <math>L_\psi</math>:

:<math>\psi(r) = -\frac{G_\psi Q_\psi}{r}\,e^{-r/L_\psi}</math>

This is the Yukawa potential — the same form derived for the static limit in [[ψ Green's Functions]] (A6) and measured in nuclear physics as the range of the nuclear force.

Key spatial regimes:

{| class="wikitable" style="width:100%;"
! Range !! Behaviour !! Engineering interpretation
|-
| <math>r \ll L_\psi</math> || <math>\psi \approx -G_\psi Q_\psi/r</math> — Coulomb-like, slow <math>1/r</math> decay || Near-field: operator's skull surface, device inner wall. Full field strength available.
|-
| <math>r \sim L_\psi</math> || <math>\psi \approx -G_\psi Q_\psi/r \cdot e^{-1} \approx 0.37\,\psi(L_\psi)</math> — field reduced to 37% || At the coherence length: field still significant but decaying. Design resonator so that shell inner surface is at <math>r \leq L_\psi</math>.
|-
| <math>r = 3L_\psi</math> || <math>\psi \approx 0.05\,\psi(L_\psi/r)</math> — less than 5% of near-field value || Beyond 3× coherence length: field negligible. External leakage from [[Psi Stabilizer]] is < 5% at distance > 60 cm.
|-
| <math>r \gg L_\psi</math> || Exponentially suppressed — effectively zero || Far-field: bystanders, environment. ψ exposure negligible.
|}

=== Anatomical Targeting ===

The choice of <math>L_\psi = 20</math> cm for the [[Psi Stabilizer]] is not arbitrary. The human temporal lobe — the primary anatomical target of the ψ₀₁₀ mode (from [[ψ Boundary Conditions]] A5) — lies approximately 15–20 cm from the centre of the head. With <math>L_\psi = 20</math> cm, the Yukawa field at the temporal lobe surface is:

:<math>\frac{\psi(15\,\text{cm})}{\psi(0^+)} \approx \frac{1}{15/20}\,e^{-15/20} \approx \frac{20}{15} \times 0.472 \approx 0.63</math>

63% of the source field amplitude reaches the temporal lobe — far above the 5% far-field threshold. Reducing <math>L_\psi</math> much below 15 cm would exponentially suppress temporal lobe coupling.

== Engineering the Coherence Length: Three Levers ==

=== Lever 1 — Ferrofluid H-field (Primary, Dynamic) ===

As derived in [[ψ Permeability]] (B3), <math>\mu_\psi(H)</math> is tunable via the ferrofluid Langevin response. Since <math>L_\psi \propto 1/\sqrt{\mu_\psi}</math>:

:<math>L_\psi(H) = L_\psi(H=0)\,/\,\sqrt{\mu_\psi(H)/\mu_0}</math>

The full H-field to L_ψ tuning curve, combined from the Langevin model and the material formula:

{| class="wikitable" style="width:100%;"
! H-field (A/m) !! <math>\mu_\psi/\mu_0</math> (composite avg.) !! <math>L_\psi</math> (relative to H=0 value) !! Target <math>L_\psi</math> (absolute) !! Mode
|-
| 0 || 1.00 || 1.00 || > 1 m || Harmonizer
|-
| 200 || 1.04 || 0.98 || ~20 cm || Stabilizer
|-
| 500 || 1.09 || 0.96 || ~18 cm || Stabilizer (tightened)
|-
