The closest physical analogue to L_ψ is the London penetration depth <math>\lambda_L</math> in superconductors. Both are determined by an effective mass term in the same type of wave equation; both set the spatial scale over which the field is screened by the medium; both are controlled by material parameters (superconducting condensate density for London depth; ferrofluid μ_ψ for L_ψ). The London depth can be tuned by changing temperature (condensate density varies); L_ψ is tuned by changing the ferrofluid H-field. The engineering philosophy is structurally identical.

