== TML Measurement Protocol ==

=== TML-1: Composite Baseline L_ψ Calibration ===

The absolute L_ψ in the composite cannot be measured directly by VNA — it requires a ψ field source and spatial field mapping. At TML-1, an indirect estimate is made by measuring the resonant frequency shift between empty and filled cavity:

:<math>\frac{\Delta\omega_{010}}{\omega_{010}} = \frac{\omega_{010}^{\rm (empty)} - \omega_{010}^{\rm (filled)}}{\omega_{010}^{\rm (empty)}} \approx 1 - \frac{1}{\sqrt{\varepsilon_\psi^{\rm eff}\mu_\psi^{\rm eff}}}</math>

This gives <math>\sqrt{\varepsilon_\psi^{\rm eff}\mu_\psi^{\rm eff}}</math> from the measured frequency shift, and therefore <math>L_\psi^{\rm mat} = L_\psi^{\rm vac}/\sqrt{\varepsilon_\psi^{\rm eff}\mu_\psi^{\rm eff}}</math> — provided <math>L_\psi^{\rm vac}</math> is known from the vacuum bare mass.

Since <math>L_\psi^{\rm vac}</math> is itself a TBD quantity (it requires knowing the ψ bare mass m), TML-1 provides the ratio <math>L_\psi^{\rm mat}/L_\psi^{\rm vac}</math> rather than the absolute value. The absolute value is a TML-3 measurement target.

=== TML-3: Direct L_ψ Spatial Measurement ===

With operator present and [[Psi Stabilizer]] in standby (no drive):

# Establish OPM sensor array at five radial distances from the Stabilizer shell surface (2, 4, 6, 8, 10 cm).
# Record OPM signal while operator maintains sustained Anchor-mode coherence (HeartMath coherence breathing).
# Fit measured field vs. distance to Yukawa profile: <math>B_{\rm OPM}(r) = A\,e^{-r/L_\psi}/r</math>.
# Extract <math>L_\psi</math> and compare against target of 20 cm.
# Repeat at baseline HRV to test nonlinear shift prediction.

'''Pass criterion:''' Measured <math>L_\psi</math> within 30% of the 20 cm target at peak HRV coherence, with the baseline L_ψ systematically longer than the coherence-state L_ψ (consistent with the nonlinear shift prediction from A3).

'''Sham control:''' Same protocol with an identical mechanical shell but no operator — measures background field profile. Any Yukawa profile should be absent in the sham condition. See [[Sham Control Design]] (F2).

== ψ-Dependent Extensions ==

=== L_ψ as an Operator Biometric ===

Within the Track B framework, a trained operator's resting L_ψ^bio is a potentially quantifiable individual biometric — analogous to resting heart rate or blood pressure. Operators with higher baseline <math>\psi_0</math> would have shorter L_ψ^bio, requiring higher ferrofluid H-field set-points for device L_ψ matching.

If L_ψ^bio correlates with training duration or meditation practice, it becomes a measurable, objective metric for psionic development — directly derivable from TML-3 spatial field mapping measurements.

=== Multi-Operator Coherence Length Contraction ===

In a [[PsiNet]] node cluster of N aligned operators, the collective background field <math>\psi_0^{\rm total} \approx N\psi_0^{\rm individual}</math> (for coherently aligned operators). The collective coherence length:

:<math>L_\psi^{\rm cluster} = \frac{1}{\sqrt{m^2 + 3\lambda N^2\psi_0^2}} \approx \frac{L_\psi^{\rm individual}}{\sqrt{N}}</math>

for large N. A group of 4 aligned operators has a collective coherence length roughly half that of a single operator. A group of 100 has one-tenth. This contraction is not a limitation — it increases the local ψ field concentration at the expense of spatial range, which is the desired effect for intense short-range group operations in [[Psi-Ops]] contexts.

